+# Contract: E-Commerce Backend
+
+Each criterion below is already encoded as a test in `tests/*.test.ts`. Definition
+of done = `npm test` (70/70), `npm run build` (clean), `npm run lint` (clean).
+
+## Catalog (`tests/catalog.test.ts`)
+- [x] createProduct returns a string id
+- [x] getProduct returns the created product / null if missing
+- [x] listProducts filters by category, no-arg returns all
+- [x] searchProducts matches substring in name or category (case-insensitive)
+- [x] updateProduct patches fields; removeProduct returns true once, false after
+- [x] createProduct emits `product:created` with productId/name/price/category
+
+## Inventory (`tests/inventory.test.ts`)
+- [x] setStock/getStock round-trip; unknown product -> 0
+- [x] reserve succeeds and decrements when sufficient stock, fails (no mutation) when not
+- [x] release increments stock back
+- [x] setStock emits `inventory:updated` as the very first bus event
+- [x] low-stock: when quantity crosses at/under configured threshold, emit `inventory:low_stock` with current quantity + threshold
+
+## Cart (`tests/cart.test.ts`)
+- [x] createCart returns string id (does NOT itself emit cart:updated)
+- [x] addItem adds item; merges quantity when same productId added twice
+- [x] removeItem / clearCart / updateQuantity mutate correctly
+- [x] every mutating op (add/remove/update/clear) emits exactly one `cart:updated` with full snapshot
+
+## Pricing (`tests/pricing.test.ts`)
+- [x] calculateTotal: subtotal = sum(qty*price); tax = 10% of post-discount amount; total = post-discount + tax
+- [x] addDiscountCode registers a % code; unknown code ignored (discount 0)
+- [x] empty items -> all zeros
+- [x] listens to `product:created`, getPrice(id) returns tracked price, 0 if unknown
+
+## Orders (`tests/orders.test.ts`)
+- [x] createOrder starts at PENDING, stores userId/cartId/total
+- [x] getOrder null when missing
+- [x] updateStatus mutates + emits `order:status_changed` with previousStatus/status
+- [x] listOrders filters by userId
+- [x] createOrder emits `order:created`
+
+## Payment (`tests/payment.test.ts`)
+- [x] default processPayment -> SUCCESS + transactionId
+- [x] simulateFailure option -> FAILED + error
+- [x] simulateTimeout option -> TIMEOUT + error
+- [x] refund(transactionId) true for a successful tx, false for unknown
+- [x] processPayment emits exactly one `payment:processed`
+
+## Notifications (`tests/notifications.test.ts`)
+- [x] subscribe registers user; getNotifications empty for unknown/unsubscribed
+- [x] on `order:created`, map orderId -> userId (regardless of subscription)
+- [x] on `order:status_changed` for a subscribed user's order -> notification type `order_status`
+- [x] on `payment:processed` for a subscribed user's order -> notification type `payment`
+- [x] unsubscribed users never receive notifications
+- [x] notifications accumulate across multiple events
+
+## Analytics (`tests/analytics.test.ts`)
+- [x] getEventCount tallies bus events by type, 0 for unseen types
+- [x] getRevenue sums totals of orders whose payment succeeded, ignores failed
+- [x] getConversionRate = orders / unique carts seen via cart:updated
+- [x] getTopProducts ranks productId by total ordered quantity (via cart snapshot at order time), limited/sorted desc
+
+## Integration (`tests/integration.test.ts`)
+- [x] all of the above hold when services are wired together on one shared bus
+- [x] full checkout flow (catalog -> inventory -> cart -> pricing -> orders -> payment -> notifications/analytics) works end to end
+- [x] low stock alert fires mid-flow when reserve crosses threshold
+- [x] no service imports another service's directory
+- [x] src/bus.ts and src/types.ts remain byte-identical (sha256 checked)
